<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    THE EIGHTH DAY - traders.xml
    ============================
    Trader stock for the new production chain.

    *** THE WRIT STOCK BELOW IS A 0.1 PLACEHOLDER. ***

    A Calling is meant to be EARNED through its Proving quest chain - trader-issued work
    that makes you actually do the discipline before it opens up. Those chains land in
    0.2 and the Writs disappear with them.

    Until then the Writs are sold at a deliberately punishing price so the Calling system
    can be tested without becoming a shopping trip. They are the one part of this mod that
    is not the design - do not balance around them.

    VERIFY-2: confirm these vanilla trader group names still exist in V3.2.
-->
<configs>

    <!-- ==========================================================================
         CALLING WRITS - NO LONGER SOLD

         0.1 sold Writs here as a placeholder so the Calling system could be
         tested before the Proving chains existed. The Provings landed in 0.2
         (see quests.xml), so the stock is gone and a Writ is now obtainable
         only by completing a Proving.

         This is deliberate and load-bearing: a Calling that can be bought is a
         purchase, and the entire pillar rests on it being work. Do not add
         Writs back to trader stock, to loot, or to any recipe.
         ========================================================================== -->


    <!-- ==========================================================================
         PRODUCTION STOCK

         Traders sell the intermediates in small quantities at bad prices. This is
         the pressure valve for a player whose chain has stalled on one missing
         input - never a substitute for building the chain.
         ========================================================================== -->

    <append xpath="/traders/trader_items">

        <trader_item_group name="edProductionStock">
            <item name="edResourceFlux" count="10,30" />
            <item name="edResourceReagentBase" count="2,6" />
            <item name="edResourcePrecisionParts" count="1,3" />
        </trader_item_group>

    </append>

</configs>
